I would probably have more items out (e.g., spare /oTel, so I didn't
have to open a bag to get a fresh one), but only one real quibble: I
wouldn't carry a pickaxe. There's a guaranteed one on Earth, which is
the only place one would need it; there are also plenty of /oDig. Not
carrying one saves a lot of weight; if I did carry one, I'd keep it in
my BoH unless I was using it at the moment.
>
>OK, that's 23 items.  Of those, there are only seven whose status is
>likely to be irrelevant (reserve bag, body armour, shirt, helm, boots,
>cloak, quest artifact; lamp state doesn't matter *much*, but relighting
>a cursed lamp after getting vortexed is a pain; yes, a lamp *is* useful
>in the endgame).  

I look at it differently. Many of the items will be blessed as a
matter of course before the endgame (armor from b?oEA, weapons from
b?oEW, BoH, unihorns, luckstone) even though they might not need to be
blessed to be effective. Amulets and rings are only a problem being
cursed when you need to take them off, which should be seldom toward
the end (possibly to get across water on Juiblex and Medusa). Cursed
wands may explode, but it's only a 1% chance. It doesn't matter if the
invocation items are cursed until you actually have to do the
invocation, at which point you can quickly take care of the problem.

And any time you need to read a b?oRC, you're taking care of _all_ of
the curse problems you have, not just the one you happen to need taken
care of at the moment. So really, for me, the issue is not what items
do you not want cursed, it's what items must remain blessed, and the
only ones that I can see are the BoH and the unihorn.

